# Testing discipline

Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) [Testing expectations](../../AGENTS.md#testing-expectations) and [`docs/testing.md`](../../docs/testing.md#when-to-add-or-update-tests).

## Authoring tests (not only running them)

- Before a PR: run `make test`, `make test-run`, and `make test-unit` (or `make test-all`).
- When you add or change **public** gameplay APIs in coverage-scope `src/*.c`, add or update tests in the matching `tests/unit/unit_*.c` (module map in `docs/testing.md`).
- PR **Test plan** must list tests added or updated, or one sentence why none.

## Module map (quick reference)

| `src` | `tests/unit` |
|-------|----------------|
| `command` | `unit_cmd.c` |
| `invent` | `unit_inv.c` |
| `combat` | `unit_cbt.c` |
| `game` | `unit_game.c` |
| `genc` | `unit_genc.c` |
| `wanderer` | `unit_wandr.c` |
| `dialogue` | `unit_dial.c` |
| `gatmos` | `unit_gatmos.c` |
| `world` | `unit_wrld.c` |
| `gprog` | `unit_gprog.c` |
| `items` | `unit_item.c` |
| `testharn` | `unit_tharn.c` |

## Determinism

- Use `unit_game_fresh` / `game_reset_fixture_baseline` and `plat_seed_rng` in unit setup.
- Use `game_roll_inject_*` and `CFG_TEST_*` for asserted combat, intimidate, and loot outcomes.
- Prefer `@fixture` in snapshots instead of RNG-walking setup (see `docs/testing.md`).

## Greatest naming

Do not name a `TEST` after a function you are testing if that collides with the C symbol (example: `TEST wanderer_cmd_reply` vs `wanderer_cmd_reply()` - use `wanderer_reply_cmd_explore` instead).
